# Google reviews on /review.
#
# Without these the page shows the two reviews the villa published itself,
# which is what it did before. With them it shows the reviews on their Google
# listing, refreshed once a day.
#
# Set them in Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment Variables), never in a
# file that is committed. Neither name has NEXT_PUBLIC_, so neither reaches the
# browser bundle; the key is used from the server only.
#
#   1. console.cloud.google.com → a project → enable billing
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Places API (New)"
#   3. Credentials → create an API key
#   4. Restrict it to the Places API. Do NOT restrict by HTTP referrer: the
#      call comes from the server, which sends no referrer.
#   5. Worth doing: APIs & Services -> Places API -> Quotas, and cap requests
#      per day at something like 100. Nothing here should ever approach that,
#      so the cap costs nothing and turns a runaway bug into an empty section
#      rather than a bill.
#
# COST. Reviews and rating sit in Google's "Place Details Enterprise" bucket:
# 1,000 calls a month free, then $20 per thousand. The page refreshes daily,
# so it uses tens of calls a month, not thousands. Check Google's pricing page
# before relying on these figures; they change them.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Optional. Without it the listing is looked up by name once per refresh. That
# lookup is on Google's unlimited free tier, so this saves a request rather than
# money — but set it anyway to pin the page to one listing, which will matter
# when the villa merges their duplicate.
GOOGLE_PLACES_PLACE_ID=
